translated_text:
CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 12
Every victim has the right to:
a. have their dignity and worth as a human being respected;
b. obtain health and psychological recovery;
c. determine their own decisions;
d. obtain information;
e. obtain special handling related to victim confidentiality;
f. obtain restitution;
g. obtain social rehabilitation;
h. obtain complaint handling services;
- 9 -
i. obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and/or
j. obtain assistance at every level of the process in accordance with statutory provisions.

text:
Pasal 13
( 1) Anak sebagai korban kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 12, juga mendapatkan  hak khusus sebagai berikut:
a. hak penghormatan atas kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh  dan berkembang;
b. hak pelayanan dasar;
c. hak perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan/atau
e. hak mendapatkan kebebasan.
(2) Dalam hal Anak sebagai pelaku kekerasan seksual atau  pelaku tindak pidana, anak berhak mendapatkan bantuan  hukum dan bantuan lainnya serta mendapatkan  penanganan khusus berkaitan dengan kerahasiaan  identitasnya.

translated_text:
Article 13
(1) Children as victims of violence, in addition to obtaining rights as referred to in Article 12, also obtain special rights as follows:
a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
e. the right to obtain freedom.
(2) In the event that a Child is a perpetrator of sexual violence or a perpetrator of a criminal act, the child has the right to obtain legal assistance and other assistance as well as to receive special handling related to the confidentiality of their identity.

text:
Pasal 14
(1) Pemerintah Daerah berkewajiban dan bertanggung jawab  untuk melaksanakan upaya perlindungan korban.  (2) Upaya perlindungan korban sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) dilakukan melalui:
a. pembentukan UPTD-PPA;
b. penetapan kebijakan;
c. penyusunan rencana program dan kegiatan;
d. pemberian dukungan sarana dan prasarana;
e. pengawasan penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap  korban sesuai standar pelayanan minimal; dan
f. pengalokasian anggaran.
(3) Dalam melaksanakan kewajiban dan tangguung jawab  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), Pemerintah Daerah  menyusun Rencana Aksi Daerah untuk perlindungan  korban.
(4) Rencana Aksi Daerah untuk  sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  Peraturan Bupati.
perlindungan  (4) ditetapkan korban  dengan - 10­ Pasa\ 15 Dalam melaksanakan kewajiban dan tanggung jawab  Pemerintah Daerah sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 14,  Bupati memberikan wewenang kepada SKPD yang mempunyai  tugas dan fungsi di bidang pemberdayaan perempuan dan  perlindungan anak.

translated_text:
Article 14
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility to implement victim protection efforts.
(2) Victim protection efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out through:
a. establishment of UPTD-PPA;
b. policy determination;
c. preparation of program and activity plans;
d. provision of facilities and infrastructure support;
e. supervision of service delivery to victims in accordance with minimum service standards; and
f. budget allocation.
(3) In carrying out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall prepare a Regional Action Plan for victim protection.
(4) The Regional Action Plan for victim protection as referred to in paragraph (4) shall be stipulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 15
In carrying out the obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 14, the Regent shall grant authority to the SKPD that has duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

text:
Pasal 16
Dalam upaya perlindungan korban, masyarakat dan keluarga  mempunyai kewajiban dan tanggung jawab sebagai berikut:  a. mencegah terjadinya kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan  anak;
b. melaporkan bila terjadi kekerasan;
c. melindungi korban; dan
d. membetikan pertolongan darurat.

translated_text:
Article 16
In efforts to protect victims, the community and family have the following obligations and responsibilities:
a. prevent the occurrence of violence against women and children;
b. report if violence occurs;
c. protect victims; and
d. provide emergency assistance.

Article 17
(1) Prevention of violence against women and children is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government coordinated by regional apparatus that has the main duties and functions of coordination in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention efforts as referred to in paragraph (1) are implemented by:
a. establishing a working network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. providing counseling/guidance;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. providing critical education about the rights of women and children for the community.

text:
Pasal 18
( 1) Pencegahan terjadinya kekerasan terhadap perempuan clan  anak sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal I 7 dilaksanakan  oleh Perangkat Dae rah dan UPTD yang tu gas pokok dan  fungsinya di bidang:
a. pendidikan;
- 11­
b. kesehatan;
c. sosial;
d. tenaga kerja;
e. pemberdayaan perempuan dan perlindungan anak; dan  f. ketenteraman dan ketertiban.
(2) Pencegahan terjadinya kekerasan oleh Perangkat Daerah dan  UPTD sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) dilaksanakan  secara terpadu dan berkesinambungan berdasarkan  petunjuk teknis dalam Rencana Aksi Daerah.

translated_text:
Article 18
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 17 shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus and UPTD whose main duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. education;
- 11-
b. health;
c. social affairs;
d. labor;
e. women's empowerment and child protection; and f. peace and order.
(2) Prevention of the occurrence of violence by Regional Apparatus and UPTD as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated and continuous manner based on technical guidelines in the Regional Action Plan.

text:
Pasal 20
(1) Pelayanan terhadap korban sebagaimana dimaksud dalam  Pasal 19, meliputi:
a. pe\ayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling;  b. pelayanan pendampingan;
c. pelayanan Kesehatan;
d. pelayanan rehabilitasi sosial;
e. pelayanan bantuan hukum;
f. pelayanan psikologis; dan
g. pelayanan pemulangan dan reintegrasi sosial.
(2) Bentuk pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat ( 1)  dilaksanakan oleh UPTD-PPA dan dapat bekerja sama  dengan Perangkat Daerah terkait dan masyarakat.

translated_text:
Article 20
(1) Services for victims as referred to in Article 19, include:
a. complaint services, consultation, and counseling;
b. assistance services;
c. health services;
d. social rehabilitation services;
e. legal aid services;
f. psychological services; and
g. repatriation and social reintegration services.
(2) The form of services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by UPTD-PPA and may cooperate with related Regional Apparatus and the community.

text:
Pasal 21
(1) Pelayanan pengaduan, konsultasi, dan konseling  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 huruf a dilakukan  oleh UPTD-PPA untuk menindaklanjuti laporan adanya  tindak kekerasan terhadap perempuan dan anak yang  diajukan korban, keluarga atau masyarakat.
(2) Pelayanan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) berupa:  a. wawancara dan opservasi keadaan korban;
b. identifikasi atau pencatatan awal korban;
- 12 ­
c. persetujuan untuk dilakukan tindakan;
d. rekomendasi layanan lanjutan;
e. koordinasi dan rujukan ke layanan lanjutan dan pihak  terkait; dan
f. pengadministrasian proses pengaduan.

translated_text:
Article 21
(1) Complaint, consultation, and counseling services as referred to in Article 20 letter a shall be conducted by UPTD-PPA to follow up on reports of acts of violence against women and children submitted by victims, families or the community.
(2) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. interviews and observation of the victim's condition;
b. initial identification or recording of the victim;
- 12 -
c. consent for action to be taken;
d. recommendation for follow-up services;
e. coordination and referral to follow-up services and related parties; and
f. administration of the complaint process.

text:
Pasal 22
Pelayanan pendampingan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal  20 ayat (1) hurufb, meliputi:
a. mendampingi korban selama proses pemeriksaan dan  pemulihan kesehatan;
b. mendampingi korban selama proses medico-legal;  c. mendampingi korban selama proses mediasi, pemeriksaan di  Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;
d. memantau kepentingan dan hak-hak korban dalam proses  pemeriksaan di Kepolisian, Kejaksaan dan Pengadilan;  e. menjaga privasi dan keharasiaan korban dari semua pihak  yang tidak berkepentingan, termasuk pemberitaan oleh  media massa;
f. melakukan koordinasi dengan pendamping yang lain; dan  g. memberikan penanganan yang bekelanjutan hingga tahap  rehabilitasi.

translated_text:
Article 22
Accompaniment services as referred to in Article 20 paragraph (1) letter b, include:
a. accompanying victims during the examination and health recovery process;
b. accompanying victims during the medico-legal process;
c. accompanying victims during the mediation process, examination at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
d. monitoring the interests and rights of victims in the examination process at the Police, Prosecutor's Office and Court;
e. protecting the privacy and confidentiality of victims from all parties who have no interest, including coverage by mass media;
f. coordinating with other companions; and
g. providing continuous handling up to the rehabilitation stage.

text:
Pasal 23
(1) Pelayanan Kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal  20 huruf c merupakan upaya yang meliputi aspek promotif,  preventif, kuratif dan rehabilitatif baik untuk pelayanan  kesehatan dasar maupun rujukan.
(2) Pelayanan kesehatan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (I)  meliputi:
a. pertolongan pertama kepada korban;
b. pemeriksaan dan pengobatan;
c. pemeriksaan lanjutan terhadap korban;
d. koordinasi pelaksanaan rehabilitasi kesehatan;  e. pemeriksaan medico-legal meliputi pengumpulan barang  bukti pada korban dan pembuatan visum et repertum;  f. pemeriksaan penunjang dan laboratorium terhadap  barang bukti;
g. konsultasi dokter ahli atau melakukan rujukan; dan  h. pelaporan kasus.

translated_text:
Article 23
(1) Health Services as referred to in Article 20 letter c constitute efforts that include promotive, preventive, curative and rehabilitative aspects for both basic health services and referral.
(2) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1) include:
a. first aid to victims;
b. examination and treatment;
c. follow-up examination of victims;
d. coordination of health rehabilitation implementation;
e. medico-legal examination including collection of evidence from victims and preparation of visum et repertum;
f. supporting examination and laboratory testing of evidence;
g. specialist doctor consultation or making referrals; and
h. case reporting.

text:
Pasal 27
(1) Penyelenggaraan pelayanan terhadap korban sebagaimana  dimaksud dalam Pasal 20 dilaksanakan dengan prinsip:  a. cepat;
b. aman dan nyaman;
c. rasa empati;
d. non diskriminasi;
e. mudah dijangkau;
f. tidak dikenakan biaya; dan
g. dijamin kerahasiannya.
(2) Penyelenggara atau pengelola pelayanan dilarang memungut  biaya apapun terhadap korban.
- 14 ­

translated_text:
Article 27
(1) The provision of services to victims as referred to in Article 20 shall be implemented with the principles of:
a. swift;
b. safe and comfortable;
c. sense of empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible;
f. not subject to fees; and
g. guaranteed confidentiality.
(2) Service providers or service managers are prohibited from collecting any fees from victims.
- 14 -

text:
Pasal 28
Bentuk pemberdayaan perempuan korban kekerasan meliputi:  a. pelatihan kerja;
b. usaha ekonomi produktif dan kelompok usaha bersama; dan  c. bantuan permodalan.

Pasal 30
Usaha ekonomi produktif dan kelompok usaha bersama  sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Pasal 28 hurufb, meliputi:  a. pelatihan ketrampilan wirausaha;
b. fasilitasi pembentukan kelompok usaha bersama; dan  c. pendarnpingan pelaksanaan usaha.

Pasal 33
(1) Pemenuhan hak anak dilaksanakan secara terpadu dan  sistematis dari seluruh sektor secara berkelanjutan melalui  kebijakan pengembangan KLA.
- 15­ {2) Kebijakan pengembangan KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) memuat ten tang:
a. konsep KLA;
b. hak anak; dan
c. pendekatan pengembangan KLA.
(3) Kebijakan pengembangan KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada  ayat (1) diarahkan pada pemenuhan hak anak, meliputi:  a. hak sipil dan kebebasan;
b. lingkungan keluarga dan pengasuhan alternatif;  c. kesehatan dasar dan kesejahteraan;
d. pendidikan, pemanfaatan waktu luang, dan kegiatan  budaya; dan
e. perlindungan khusus.
(4) Tahap pengembangan KLA sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat  (1), meliputi:
a. persiapan;
b. perencanaan;
c. pelaksanaan;
d. pemantauan;
e. evaluasi; dan
f. pelaporan.
(SJ Ketentuan lebih lanjut mengenai kebijakan pengembangan  KLA diatur dengan Peraturan Bupati.

translated_text:
Article 33
(1) The fulfillment of children's rights is implemented in an integrated and systematic manner from all sectors on a sustainable basis through the KLA development policy.
- 15­ (2) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) contains provisions regarding:
a. the KLA concept;
b. children's rights; and
c. the KLA development approach.
(3) The KLA development policy as referred to in paragraph (1) is directed toward the fulfillment of children's rights, comprising:
a. civil rights and freedoms;
b. family environment and alternative care;
c. basic health and welfare;
d. education, utilization of leisure time, and cultural activities; and
e. special protection.
(4) The stages of KLA development as referred to in paragraph (1), comprise:
a. preparation;
b. planning;
c. implementation;
d. monitoring;
